# oracle: pair_style pace with the .yace potential of the LAMMPS example PACKAGES/dispersion (c_ace.yace: ChebExpCos, 2 densities, the distance inner cutoff rcut_in 0.7 dcut_in 0.1 that switches the radial basis and the core repulsion) on a 2x2x2 diamond cell with displaced atoms: run 0 with one pair at 0.65 Angstrom (inside the switching range; forces dumped), then that atom moved away and 20 NVE steps
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE; see w257pace_recursive)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.3e-14, atoms 3.1e-14 (the run 0 forces at 0.65 Angstrom included).
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/dispersion/potential_files/c_ace.yace
# oracle-files: w270ya_pace_yace_c.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all filerel=1e-10
units       metal
atom_style  atomic
lattice     diamond 3.567
region      box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box  1 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass        1 12.011
displace_atoms all random 0.05 0.05 0.05 7741 units box
set         atom 2 x 0.65 y 0.0 z 0.0
set         atom 1 x 0.0 y 0.0 z 0.0
pair_style  pace
pair_coeff  * * c_ace.yace C
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxy
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run         0
write_dump  all custom w270ya_pace_yace_c.dump id fx fy fz modify format float %.15g sort id
set         atom 2 x 0.9 y 0.9 z 0.0
velocity    all create 300 4928459 rot yes dist gaussian
fix         1 all nve
timestep    0.0002
thermo      5
run         20
